# Local development only. Copy to apps/wolf/.env.local and do not commit that copy.
# next dev, and the db:migrate, db:seed:dev, and db:provision commands, accept only
# 127.0.0.1 port 5433 database wolf_command. They do not rewrite another URL.
# NODE_ENV=production does not accept this local URL. See docs/database-configuration.md.
# The database commands load apps/wolf/.env.local themselves and never write it.
# Variables already set in the environment are kept and then validated.
# next dev, next start, and next build load this file through Next.js.
# These values are placeholders for the Docker Compose Postgres service.
# Do not put production credentials, service-account keys, or real API keys here.
# Wolf passwords are separate from email-provider passwords. Do not put those here.

DATABASE_URL=postgresql://wolf:wolf@127.0.0.1:5433/wolf_command

# Optional. Set to 1 to mark the session cookie Secure outside production.
# WOLF_COOKIE_SECURE=0

# Development seed and account provisioning are refused when NODE_ENV=production.
# WOLF_ALLOW_DEV_SEED=1
# WOLF_ALLOW_ACCOUNT_PROVISION=1
# WOLF_PROVISION_EMAIL=
# WOLF_PROVISION_PASSWORD=
# WOLF_PROVISION_MODE=create
# WOLF_PROVISION_COMPANY=
# WOLF_PROVISION_DEPARTMENT=
# WOLF_PROVISION_ROLE=
# WOLF_PROVISION_OWNER_PRIVATE=0
